        "original_id": "6231466b-dfa3-5b67-b1c7-8a1f48c95684",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: EdChoice, Cato Institute Center for Educational Freedom\n- People: Milton Friedman, Rose Director Friedman, Jason Bedrick\n- Roles: Founder, Director of Policy, adjunct scholar, policy analyst\n- Topics: Economics, educational policy\n\nFacts:\n- Milton Friedman was an American economist born on July 31, 1912, and he died on November 16, 2006.\n- Milton Friedman received the 1976 Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences for research on consumption analysis, monetary history and theory, and the complexity of stabilization policy.\n- EdChoice was founded in 1996 by Milton Friedman and his wife, economist Rose Director Friedman.\n- Jason Bedrick is the Director of Policy at EdChoice.\n- Jason Bedrick is an adjunct scholar at the Cato Institute's Center for Educational Freedom.\n- Jason Bedrick previously worked as a policy analyst at the Cato Institute's Center for Educational Freedom.",
